--TEST--
an expression `catch` arm's body is an expression, so `return` is refused and the block form is named — `rule:expressions/catch-arm-is-an-expression`'s E0126
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:expressions/catch-arm-is-an-expression`: the arm is parsed as an expression and that is the whole
// rule. `throw` is admitted because `throw expr` already is one; `return`,
// `break` and `continue` are statements, so they are named here rather than
// left to a generic expected-expression error.
uint $count = Core\Str::length("hi") catch (RuntimeError $e) => return Core\Str::length("");
echo $count, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0126]: a `catch` arm is an expression, and `return` is a statement
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
